[00:00.32] They disembarked in '45
[00:03.81] And no one spoke and no one smiled
[00:08.99] There were too many spaces in the line
[00:14.43] 
[00:17.31] Gathered at the cenotaph
[00:22.23] All agreed with hand on heart
[00:27.57] To sheath the sacrificial knives
[00:31.75] (Thats right)
[00:33.72] But now
[00:35.42] She stands upon Southampton dock
[00:38.98] With her handkerchief
[00:41.69] And her summer frock
[00:44.60] Clings to her wet body in the rain
[00:51.13] In quiet desperation knuckles
[00:56.06] White upon the slippery reins
[01:01.26] She bravely waves the boys goodbye again
[01:08.71] 
[01:22.49] Still the dark stain spreads between
[01:27.02] Their shoulder blades
[01:30.32] 
[01:33.78] A mute reminder of the poppy fields and graves
[01:43.31] 
[01:45.88] When the fight was over
[01:50.66] We spent what they had made
[01:56.33] But in the bottom of our hearts
[02:00.33] We felt the final cut
[02:02.40] 